WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.834
-Welcome back to the show.
I appreciate you coming on.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:04.601
-I'm so happy
to be here in person.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:05.801
-Yeah.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.667
-It's like wearing a suit
and, like, hard clothing.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.033
It's actually so nice.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.501
It doesn't sound like it
would be, but it really is.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:12.834
-Yeah, you're not Zooming.
Yeah.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:13.834
-Yeah.
-You look great, by the way.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.033
I like that suit.
-Thanks. You too.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.067
-I want to congratulate
you on --

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.701
You just won an Emmy like
yesterday or the day before.

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:19.834
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.434
-"Queer Eye."
Congratulations!

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:26.801
-And what's so exciting is,
it's really an award for --

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.801
'Cause it was
Best Unscripted Series,

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.634
so it's really, like -- It's
an award for everybody, right?

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:32.701
It's like every single person
of production

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.167
really got to, like, enjoy it,
which is really nice.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.334
-It's so well-done.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.968
-Four years running,
which is, like, crazy.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:40.234
-It really is, right?

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:41.467
Congrats on that.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:44.367
You have all sorts of
good tips in this book.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.400
Just looking at
some of these photos,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.200
you go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.200
I would just eat every single
thing in this here.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.868
Oh, my God. It's so good.
I just, like --

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.067
-Thank you.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.067
-I gain 20 pounds just by
looking at it, but --

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.968
-But it's all healthy-ish.
-It is healthy, by the way.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.100
-Most of it.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.634
-But what is the --
What's the reason for --

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.234
This is your second cookbook.

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:05.033
The first one was just recipes
that you learned growing up?

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:07.033
-Pretty much. Like, I think --
-I have that one, as well.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.534
-"Antoni in the Kitchen"
was basically like

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.734
a culinary memoir of,
like, dishes that shaped me,

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:11.901
my Polish heritage,

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.534
dishes that didn't make it
on to "Queer Eye"

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.567
that I was a little salty about,

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.567
so I wanted to throw them
into a book.

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.734
-That's right.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.601
-And with "Let's Do Dinner,"
it's really --

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.434
You know, the irony of the life
that I have now is,

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:21.801
I don't -- pandemic aside,

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.200
I don't have as much time
in the kitchen,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.834
but I still want to have
meaningful, good food,

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.534
but I just don't have
as much time to make it.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.934
So this book is
a reflection of that.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.801
-I follow you on
all the socials and stuff.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.267
You know I'm a big fan of you.
-Ditto.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:35.834
-And I saw a lot of bookstores
really getting behind you

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.033
and supporting
"Let's Do Dinner."

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:41.601
And this one bookstore --
I guess you sent out

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.667
cardboard cutouts of you
to these --

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.901
-Okay, I need to clarify.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:49.634
I did not send out
life-size cutouts of myself.

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:51.133
-Yeah, but someone must have.
-The publisher.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.634
-Alright, well --

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:55.934
-My publisher decided it was a
thing that was going to happen,

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.667
and I went with it
because I'm Canadian,

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:02.000
and we're not combative
and we just, like --

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.801
We just say -- We "Yes and..."

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.200
-Yes and...
Obviously.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.767
But this is at
the Blue Willow Bookshop

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.334
in Houston, Texas.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:13.601
This is you hanging out with --
in front the bookstore there.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.801
-I remember that day
with great fondness.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.400
-Yeah, you were outside all day.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.501
-I showed up with
my smoked-trout Nicoise

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:23.267
and perfect jammy eggs
in a mohair sweater and jeans

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.701
and I just waited outside
of Blue Willow Bookshop.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.667
-Yeah. And then --
-As one does.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.033
-And then here's you at the

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.367
Country Bookshop in
Bozeman, Montana.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.267
-Oh, that was my two friends.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:35.834
-Yeah. You remember meeting
them, as well?

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.267
-I really remember, yeah.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:40.300
-Well, I was thinking, why --
It's fun to just have

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.234
one Antoni here, but why not
have two Antonis out here?

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:47.100
I thought if we have --
Do we have the other Antoni?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.234
There you are. Here.

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:57.567
How does it compare to
the real -- Can you --

00:02:57.567 --> 00:03:00.601
I mean, it's really legit.
It's real. It's bizarre.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.667
-It's terrifying.
-No, it is not.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.133
-There's nothing
natural about it.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:07.267
-No, I was wondering,
would you like to autograph it,

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.534
and maybe we'll give it
to a fan?

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:09.968
Anyone --
-I would love to.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.334
Thank you.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:16.000
Do I sign on my chest?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.934
-Yeah, exactly.
♪♪

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.100
Alright, here we go. Alright.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
Here you are. Let's go.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:27.868
Bring it to somebody?
-Bringing it?

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.167
-Yeah.
-Alright.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.534
-Who wants Antoni?
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:34.133
Here we go. Do you see one?

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.634
Do you know where it's going?
Here.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.300
-It's for you.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.767
Good luck!
-Look at that.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.334
Good luck getting it home.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:44.200
Good luck.
-I'll get you an Uber.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.601
I'll get you an Uber.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:48.901
-I was gonna say, good luck
getting that on the subway.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:53.801
Guys, the book
is "Let's Do Dinner."

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.300
Antoni Porowski, everybody.
-Thank you.

